# Autonomous Business Builder

## Goal

Convert `businessIdea`, `targetMarket`, `country`, `budget` into: Market Analysis, Branding, Landing Page copy, Marketing Content, Sales Strategy, Analytics (KPIs/roadmap).

## Stack

- Frontend: `frontend/` — Next.js 15, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind
- Backend: `backend/app/` — FastAPI, SQLAlchemy async, Alembic, PostgreSQL JSONB
- AI: OpenAI via `BaseAgent`; `OPENAI_API_KEY=mock` → `_mock_output()` with `prior_results`
- DB default: `sqlite+aiosqlite:///./business_builder.db` (Docker uses Postgres)
- Validate agent JSON via `app/agent_outputs.py` before save
- Pipeline: `app/services/agent_pipeline.py`

## Layout

```
backend/app/
  main.py, models.py, schemas.py, database.py, config.py
  routers/   projects.py, agents.py, results.py
  agents/    base_agent.py, market_agent.py, branding_agent.py,
             content_agent.py, sales_agent.py, analytics_agent.py
frontend/src/
  app/           page.tsx, new-business/, projects/, results/[id]/
  components/    Navbar, AgentCard, ProgressTracker, ResultsPanel
  lib/api.ts     types/index.ts
```

## Models

- `BusinessProject`: id, business_idea, target_market, country, budget, status, created_at
- `AgentResult`: id, project_id, agent_name (`market|branding|content|sales|analytics`), result_json, created_at

## API

| Method | Path | Notes |
|--------|------|-------|
| POST | `/projects` | Create project; background runs all 5 agents |
| GET | `/projects`, `/projects/{id}` | List / detail + results |
| GET | `/results/{project_id}` | Agent results only |
| POST | `/agents/run` | Single agent on demand |

## Agent pipeline

1. market → 2. branding → 3. content → 4. sales → 5. analytics. Later agents use `prior_results` from earlier steps.

New agent: subclass `BaseAgent`, implement `name`, `_system_prompt()`, `_mock_output()`, register in pipeline/router.

## Rules

- MVP only — no new deps unless required
- Backend first for API/data; frontend uses `lib/api.ts`
- JSON outputs only; validate with Pydantic schemas
- Reuse `BaseAgent`, existing routers, components
- No overengineering; prefer simple solutions
- Env: `backend/.env`, `frontend/.env.local`, root `.env` for Docker

## Build order

1. Schema/model → service/agent → router → frontend page/component
2. Test with `OPENAI_API_KEY=mock`
